--| An `indapp` expression is a spine with a variable head, so it is an expression node.
lemma i9_indapp_out (G: hyps) (M W R: class) (u t1 t2 t3 t4 t5 t6: set): $ G ⇒ ra_indapp t1 t2 t3 t4 t5 t6 ∈ lrel $ > $ G ⇒ t5 ∊ trees ω $ > $ G ⇒ ¬ R ∈ fseq u $ > $ G ⇒ dt u M t5 W R = ∅ $
----
a1: $ G ⇒ ∃ x1 ∃ x2 ∃ x3 ∃ x4 ∃ x5 ∃ x6 ∃ x7 ∃ x8 ∃ x9 ∃ x0 ∃ y (t1 = x1 ∧ t2 = x2 ∧ t3 = x3 ∧ t4 = x4 ∧ t5 = y ∧ t6 = x5 ∧ ra_spine ⟨ kc_bvar , scons x7 ∅ ⟩ y x9 ∈ lrel ∧ ra_add x4 x3 x6 ∈ lrel ∧ ra_add x6 x5 x7 ∈ lrel ∧ ra_le ⟨ kc_s , scons x5 ∅ ⟩ x2 ∈ lrel ∧ ra_pargs ⟨ kc_bvar , scons x7 ∅ ⟩ x4 x3 x0 ∈ lrel ∧ ra_nidx x1 x5 x8 ∈ lrel ∧ ra_iargs x6 x8 x0 y ∈ lrel) $ by lrel_indapp_cases [#1]
