--| A concatenation's entries grow with those of its second part (given pairwise).
lemma i9_scat_sub {i v v2: set} (G: hyps) (X1 X2: class) (p: set): $ G ⇒ ∀ i ∀ v (⟨ i , v ⟩ ∈ X1 → ∃ v2 (⟨ i , v2 ⟩ ∈ X2 ∧ v ⊆ v2)) $ > $ G ⇒ ∀ i (fv (scat p X1) i ⊆ fv (scat p X2) i) $
----
y1: $ G , q ∊ fv (scat p X1) o , r ∊ ap (scat p X1) o , q ∊ r ⇒ r ∊ ap (scat p X1) o $ by ax
y2: $ G , q ∊ fv (scat p X1) o , r ∊ ap (scat p X1) o , q ∊ r ⇒ ⟨ o , r ⟩ ∈ (scat p X1) $ by cab_elim [y1]
y3: $ G , q ∊ fv (scat p X1) o , r ∊ ap (scat p X1) o , q ∊ r , c = ⟨ o , r ⟩ , c ∊ (scat p X1) ⇒ c ∊ (scat p X1) $ by ax
y4: $ G , q ∊ fv (scat p X1) o , r ∊ ap (scat p X1) o , q ∊ r , c = ⟨ o , r ⟩ , c ∊ (scat p X1) ⇒ c ∊ p ∨ c ∊ {z | ∃ i ∃ y (z = ⟨ nadd (cdm p) i , y ⟩ ∧ ⟨ i , y ⟩ ∈ X1)} $ by cun_elim [y3]
a1: $ G , q ∊ fv (scat p X1) o , r ∊ ap (scat p X1) o , q ∊ r , c = ⟨ o , r ⟩ , c ∊ (scat p X1) , c ∊ p ⇒ c ∊ p $ by ax
a2: $ G , q ∊ fv (scat p X1) o , r ∊ ap (scat p X1) o , q ∊ r , c = ⟨ o , r ⟩ , c ∊ (scat p X1) , c ∊ p ⇒ c ∊ (scat p X2) $ by cun_intro_l [a1]
a3: $ G , q ∊ fv (scat p X1) o , r ∊ ap (scat p X1) o , q ∊ r , c = ⟨ o , r ⟩ , c ∊ (scat p X1) , c ∊ p ⇒ c = ⟨ o , r ⟩ $ by ax
a4: $ G , q ∊ fv (scat p X1) o , r ∊ ap (scat p X1) o , q ∊ r , c = ⟨ o , r ⟩ , c ∊ (scat p X1) , c ∊ p ⇒ ⟨ o , r ⟩ ∈ (scat p X2) $ by wcel_intro [a3, a2]
a5: $ G , q ∊ fv (scat p X1) o , r ∊ ap (scat p X1) o , q ∊ r , c = ⟨ o , r ⟩ , c ∊ (scat p X1) , c ∊ p ⇒ r ∊ ap (scat p X2) o $ by cab_intro [a4]
a6: $ G , q ∊ fv (scat p X1) o , r ∊ ap (scat p X1) o , q ∊ r , c = ⟨ o , r ⟩ , c ∊ (scat p X1) , c ∊ p ⇒ q ∊ r $ by ax
